{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"The rerun exposed the exact race: libtest’s own parallel `ok` output entered a redirected descriptor, producing a false mismatch. A mutex cannot cover harness output after a test returns, so I’m moving valid calls into isolated batch child processes: one child per library per configuration captures only the exported function’s bytes to a file, while the parent compares those files. This preserves randomized coverage and eliminates process-global stdout interference."}}
